  {
   "id": 639768,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/5a0f74b8a09cc472.jpg\" alt=\"In Figure X on the left is a figure showing DNA in the cytoplasm surrounded by a plasma membrane. mRNA is produced from the DNA and multiple ribosomes producing proteins are on the mRNA. In Figure Y on the right is a figure showing DNA surrounded by the nuclear membrane. Pre-mRNA is produced from the DNA, leading to mature mRNA, which is exported to the cytoplasm. Multiple ribosomes with proteins are on the exported mRNA.\"></p>\n\n<p>What do figures X and Y in the graphic illustrate?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1246598,
     "content_html": "Transcription and translation in a eukaryotic cell (figure X) and a prokaryotic cell (figure Y)."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246599,
     "content_html": "Transcription and translation in a prokaryotic cell (figure X) and a eukaryotic cell (figure Y)."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246597,
     "content_html": "Transcription in a eukaryotic cell (figure X) and translation in a prokaryotic cell (figure Y)."
    },
    {
     "id": 1246596,
     "content_html": "Transcription in a prokaryotic cell (figure X) and translation in a eukaryotic cell (figure Y)"
    }
   ],
